{title: Shady Grove}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: Am}
{tempo: 120}
{lyrics_rights: public-domain}
{genre: Traditional, Folk, Appalachian}
{source: Traditional Appalachian ballad.}
{start_of_verse}
I [Am]went to the [C]shady [G]grove
And [Am]there I did [C]find a [G]flower
It [Am]was so [C]shady and [D]sweet to behold
That [Am]I [C]could not [D]leave it [Am]alone
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse2}
I [Am]plucked that [C]flower [G]up to [Am]me
And [Am]laid it [C]on my [D]breast to [Am]be
The [Am]sweetest [C]flower [D]the [Am]sun ever [C]shone [D]on
That [Am]ever [C]bloomed [D]in the [Am]shady [C]grove [D]one
{end_of_verse2}
{start_of_chorus}
And [Am]if [C]you [G]dare to [Am]go [C]with me
To the [Am]shady [C]grove [G]you [Am]may see
It [Am]was so [C]shady and [D]sweet to behold
That [Am]I [C]could not [D]leave it [Am]alone
{end_of_chorus}
